# The address of the Stage-Server this build talks to - the one address for everything: the API, the band's
# database (through the server's own `/db` proxy, so one accepted certificate covers the app, the API and the sync)
# and, once `npm run build` has been run, the app itself.
#
# The PWA never holds an administrator login of the database: every device has its own login, made when it founds a
# band (POST /workspaces) or joins one (POST /workspaces/:id/join/:profileId) and kept as a document of the band.
#
# For tablets on the stage LAN, use the server's LAN address instead of localhost (a tablet asking for localhost
# would ask itself). https:// once `scripts/generate-dev-certs.sh` has been run: getUserMedia() and WebMIDI need a
# secure context. The server also needs the matching FRONTEND_ORIGIN for CORS - only while Vite's own dev server is
# used; once core-backend serves the build, everything is one origin.
#
# This is only the build-time default: a device can point at another Stage-Server in Einstellungen without a rebuild
# (stageServer.ts, getStageServerUrl()). stageboard.local is the mDNS name core-backend answers itself (docs/03 §0a);
# with `setcap cap_net_bind_service` on node it can listen on 443, so no port has to be written out.
VITE_STAGE_SERVER_URL=https://stageboard.local
